<title>NETHERLANDS: POLL - Dutch bond yield survey - August.</title>
<headline>POLL - Dutch bond yield survey - August.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reuters continues its monthly survey of bank economists' forecasts of levels for key Dutch interest rates in one month's time. Tabulated results follow:</p>
<p>		     3-MTH   5-YR   10-YR   LONG    5-YR   10-YR</p>
<p>							     SPREAD  SPREAD</p>
<p>							     (to Bunds, bp)</p>
<p>CURRENT	    3.42    4.80   5.63    6.34     +2	-6</p>
<p>ABN AMRO</p>
<p>HOARE GOVETT     3.50    4.85   5.70    6.40	0	-5</p>
<p>GENERALE BANK    3.50    4.75   5.55    6.25     +2	-8</p>
<p>ING BARINGS	3.40    4.80   5.60    6.30	0	-5</p>
<p>IRIS		 3.50    4.90   5.65    6.40     -3	-5</p>
<p>MEESPIERSON	3.40    4.90   5.75    6.40     +5	-3</p>
<p>RABOBANK</p>
<p>INTERNATIONAL    3.40    4.90   5.75    6.45	0	 0</p>
<p>NOTES - The relevant benchmark bonds are the 8.25 pct Feb 15,</p>
<p>2002, 5.75 pct Feb 15, 2007 and 7.50 pct Jan 5, 2023 Dutch state</p>
<p>loans (DSLs) and the 8.00 pct Jan 21, 2002 and 6.00 pct July 4,</p>
<p>2007 Bunds.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000, fax 31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
